# Shrimp Creole

Alex’s grandfather’s recipe

{ rating="5" image="shrimp_creole.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 (32 oz) can of [tomato sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" }
- [ ] 4 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" } (1/2 stick)
- [ ] 1.5 [onions]{ ing="onions" }, diced
- [ ] 1.5 stalks [celery]{ ing="celery" }, half rings (_or 1 carrot, diced_)
- [ ] 1.5 [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }
- [ ] 1 (15 oz) can [whole tomatoes]{ ing="whole-tomatoes" }, cut into quarters (with scissors)
- [ ] [Baked Spices]{ ing="baked-spices" }

      - [ ] 1 [bay leaf]{ ing="bay-leaf" }
      - [ ] 1/2 tsp [Tabasco sauce]{ ing="tabasco-sauce" }
      - [ ] 1/2 Tbsp fresh [thyme]{ ing="thyme" } (1.5 tsp dry)
- [ ] (Added after baking) 1/4 bunch [parsley]{ ing="parsley" }, chopped (1.5 tsp dry)
- [ ] 1 lbs [raw shrimp]{ ing="raw-shrimp" }, peeled and deveined
- [ ] 2 cups [white rice and saffron]{ ing="white-rice-and-saffron" } (~200 mg) _OR_ a baguette, toasted in the oven

## Recipe

1. _(Before starting, ensure the [shrimp]{ ing="raw-shrimp" } is peeled and ready and defrost if needed)_
1. Pour the can of [tomato sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" } into an enameled dutch oven. Bake uncovered for 90 min at 350 degrees
1. While reducing, dice the [onion]{ ing="onions" } and carrot. Set aside
1. With 20m remaining, melt the [butter]{ ing="butter" } in a large pan and toast the garlic until aromatic (1 min)

   1. Add the [onion]{ ing="onions" } and carrot and saute until softened
1. Once the [sauce]{ ing="tomato-sauce" } is done, restore 3/4 of the volume with water (e.g. 28 oz water for 32 oz [sauce]{ ing="tabasco-sauce" })

   1. Add the [spices]{ ing="baked-spices" }, chopped [tomatoes]{ ing="whole-tomatoes" }, and sauteed vegetables to the pot
   1. Cover the pot and return to the oven for 30 min
   1. Uncover and bake for 30 additional minutes
1. _(Can stop here to store overnight in the fridge)_
1. For the [saffron]{ ing="white-rice-and-saffron" } rice, mix rice, water, and the pinches of saffron in a rice cooker
1. On the stove top, bring the pot to a boil. Add the [parsley]{ ing="parsley" } and [shrimp]{ ing="raw-shrimp" } and cook for at most 5 min or until the shrimp reach 145 degrees
1. Serve over warm [saffron]{ ing="white-rice-and-saffron" } rice or with a side baguette

## Notes

1. Total cook time is around 3 hours
1. This recipe has been cut in half to serve 3-4 people instead of 8
1. We typically buy frozen shrimp that need to be peeled. If so, defrost overnight in the fridge so that they can be peeled before cooking
